        "body": "> Good point, I switched it to `vim.fn.getcwd(-1, -1, -1)` now.\r\n\r\nGreat, that should work wonderfully.\r\n\r\n> > if the user has an autocommand which changes the buffer-local directory (e.g. to the project root)\r\n> \r\n> That seems like it would be unusual to me. But, can close this if we wanna keep things the way they are.\r\n\r\nI mean, it's definitely a matter of opinion, but I think keeping `1-` consistent is the way to go. It's unfortunate that by default `1-` is a bit useless, but as mentioned, it's not always useless if the user is using something like `:h workspace-dir`.\r\n",
        "created_at": "2026-08-10T03:58:58Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-08-10T03:58:58Z",
